# ForgeOps repository ignores — design.md §0.3, §14.1.
#
# Ignore generated output, the local `.env` override, tool caches and IDE state.
# NEVER ignore: licence/notice files, committed lockfiles, `.env.example`, or the
# four authoritative root documents
# (AI-Powered-DevOps-Platform-Complete-Technical-Research.md, PRD.md,
# Tech-Stack-Analysis.md, phases.md). Those are tracked inputs.
# scripts/check-hygiene.sh asserts both halves of that rule.

# ─── Local environment override (design §13.1, §13.3) ────────────────────────
# `.env` is created locally by scripts/init-env.sh; `.env.example` is committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ─── Python / backend build + cache output ───────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
# Hash-pinned locks are committed (design §16.2) — never ignored.
!backend/requirements.lock
!backend/requirements-dev.lock

# ─── Go / agent build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
agent/bin/
agent/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.prof
# `go.sum` is committed (design §16.1) — never ignored.
!agent/go.sum
# pgregory.net/rapid writes a reproduction failfile under testdata/rapid/ whenever a
# property fails. It is a debugging artifact keyed to one seed and machine, not source,
# and it appears every time a Go negative control is exercised — which would break the
# mutation harness's "working tree is clean afterwards" guarantee (design §0.4.5) for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the mutation.
**/testdata/rapid/

# ─── Node / frontend build output and caches ─────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
# `pnpm-lock.yaml` is committed (design §16.3) — never ignored.
!frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml

# ─── OpenTofu working state (design §10.6, §16.4) ────────────────────────────
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tofuplan.bin
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Provider lock files are committed with six-platform checksums — never ignored.
!**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# ─── Release / supply-chain output (design §8.1–§8.2) ────────────────────────
dist/
sbom/

# ─── IDE and editor state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Local logs and scratch space ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
tmp/
.cache/
# One-shot local scratch: `*.tmp` intermediates and `scripts/_*.py` helpers that
# generate a committed artifact once and are not part of the build. A script that
# CI or a Make target invokes never carries the `_` prefix. `scripts/_*.txt` holds
# long commit messages passed to `git commit -F`, which must not themselves become
# untracked files — the mutation harness (§0.4.5) requires `git status --porcelain`
# to be empty after a run, so scratch that is not ignored would fail it.
*.tmp
# The rest of the scratch family, added 2026-08-19 after a cleanup found 202 loose files under
# `.evidence/` and a `.commitmsg.tmp` at the root. `*.tmp` alone did not cover them: captured
# command output tends to land as `.out`, `.err` or `.hits`, editors and patch tools leave `.bak`,
# `.orig` and `.rej`, and a half-written replacement lands as `.new`. None of these extensions is
# tracked anywhere in the tree, so ignoring them costs nothing and keeps
# `git status --porcelain` empty — which the mutation harness (§0.4.5) requires after a run.
*.bak
*.new
*.hits
*.err
*.out
*.orig
*.rej
scripts/_*.py
scripts/_*.sh
scripts/_*.txt
# Captured command output kept while working a task (check exit codes, test tails,
# coverage numbers). Evidence belongs in PROGRESS.md, not in loose files, so this
# directory is deliberately never committed.
/.evidence/
# The comprehension artifact's own working directory. `build-graph.mjs`,
# `semantic-overlay.json`, `README.md` and `.ua/.understandignore` are authored source and
# ARE committed. Everything else under `.ua/` is generated on every run — a 1.6 MB
# knowledge graph, a raw scan of the tree and run metadata. Committing those would put a
# second, staler copy of the repository's shape under version control and would leave
# `git status --porcelain` dirty after every regeneration, which the mutation harness
# (§0.4.5) treats as a failure. `docs/development.md` documents how to rebuild them.
docs/understand-anything/.ua/*
!docs/understand-anything/.ua/.understandignore


# Captured command output. Not covered until now, which is exactly why 18 of these accumulated
# at the repository root — 3.83 MB of pytest and agent transcripts named `agent_log4.log`,
# `auth_failed3.log`, `run_failed.log` and so on. None was ever tracked and none was ever
# wanted; the pattern was simply missing, so `git status` stayed noisy and the next person had
# to decide, every time, whether a `.log` at the root mattered.
#
# Verified safe before adding: no tracked file anywhere in the repository has a `.log`
# extension, so this pattern cannot hide something that is under version control. The four
# `.log` files the comprehension artifact writes under `.ua/intermediate/` are already covered
# by the rule above; this one catches them a second time, harmlessly.
*.log

# Personal presentation notes. `PRESENTATION-GUIDE.md` is a demo script and speaking crib
# written for one person on one day: it holds a walkthrough order, phrasing to use out loud,
# anticipated questions, and a frank list of gaps to disclose. None of that describes the
# system, so it does not belong beside `README.md`, `PROGRESS.md` or `docs/` — and unlike
# those files nothing verifies it, so a committed copy would become a fourth record that
# drifts and then contradicts the three that are gated.
#
# It also names the machine-local setup traps (`make` needs Git Bash, the `LLM_KEY_*` values
# in `.env` are placeholders), which are true of one workstation and would mislead anyone
# else who cloned the repository and read them as project documentation.
PRESENTATION-GUIDE.md

# Local development credentials. `credentials.md` lists the sign-in accounts, the Authentik admin and
# the infrastructure addresses for a stack that runs on one machine behind 127.0.0.1. None of it is a
# production secret, and all of it is recreatable from `make init-env` + `provision-authentik.py`,
# which is exactly why it should not be tracked: a committed credential file is a credential file
# whether or not the values matter, and the next person to add a real value to it will not notice
# that the rule changed.
credentials.md

# Architecture diagrams generated for the presentation, from a snapshot of the tree at one
# commit. Same reasoning as `PRESENTATION-GUIDE.md` above: nothing gates them, so a committed
# copy becomes a diagram that describes a tree it no longer matches — the exact defect this
# repository has spent five sessions correcting in `api.md`, `architecture.md` and
# `deployment.md`. They carry the commit they were read from and are meant to be regenerated,
# not maintained. Folding them into `docs/architecture.md` is fine, but only alongside a check
# that asserts every service they name still exists in `docker-compose.yml`.
ARCHITECTURE-DIAGRAMS.md
